// How it works
// - The six text fields arrive as white-on-transparent textures from Text Render nodes.
//   The first passes measure them on a 480 x 270 grid: ink coverage, then each text line
//   (up to 6 per field, split on empty rows) and, inside a line, the glyph index of each
//   column. So the layout can place and scale every line on its own (Eva justified
//   titles) and the animations can reveal whole glyphs (typing, decoding) without ever
//   cutting or distorting a letter. These passes are persistent and only rerun when the
//   text changes (plus a safety refresh every 30 frames): live cost is near zero.
// - The st pass (first) is a 2 x 1 state: preset on screen, its start time, the preset waiting to come
//   in and when it was asked. The outgoing preset plays its exit, then the cut happens.
// - The scene pass draws the preset (premultiplied), gA / gB blur it for the glow, the last
//   pass adds glow, scanlines, grain, chromatic offset, background and the transition.
// Layout is in pixels with "U" = 1 % of the short side, so every preset recomposes itself
// for 16:9, 4:3, square, portrait or ultra-wide outputs.

// ATLAS BEGIN
// generated by build_atlas.py (2048x2048)
